<title>GERMANY: German cocoa grind rises seven pct in Q3 - BDS.</title>
<headline>German cocoa grind rises seven pct in Q3 - BDS.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German cocoa grind in the third quarter of 1996 totalled 65,824 tonnes, the German Confectionery Association BDS said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>This was 7.0 percent up from 61,523 tonnes in the third quarter of 1995, a BDS statement said.</p>
<p>The figure in the second quarter of 1996 was 59,471 tonnes.</p>
<p>Traders and analysts last week forecast the German figure five percent higher, citing colder than usual weather. -Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
